{
  "id": "03914_taru",
  "headword": "{足|た}る",
  "reading": "たる",
  "part_of_speech": "godan verb",
  "gloss": "to be sufficient, to be worthy of",
  "conjugation": {
    "type": "godan",
    "ending": "る",
    "stem": "{足|た}"
  },
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to be sufficient, to be enough",
      "explanation": "To meet the requirements or standards needed."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to be worthy of, to deserve",
      "explanation": "To have the qualities needed to be considered something."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "03914_taru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{信頼|しんらい}に{足|た}る{人物|じんぶつ}だ。",
      "english": "He is a person worthy of trust.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03914_taru_ex2",
      "japanese": "この{量|りょう}で{足|た}りますか？",
      "english": "Is this amount sufficient?",
      "notes": "[Note: {足|た}りる (ichidan verb form) is more common in modern Japanese]",
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03914_taru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{行動|こうどう}は{批判|ひはん}に{足|た}る。",
      "english": "His actions deserve criticism.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03914_taru_ex4",
      "japanese": "{千円|せんえん}あれば{足|た}る。",
      "english": "A thousand yen will be enough.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03914_taru_ex5",
      "japanese": "{取|と}るに{足|た}らない{問題|もんだい}だ。",
      "english": "It's a trivial problem.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "03914_taru_ex6",
      "japanese": "{尊敬|そんけい}に{足|た}る{人物|じんぶつ}はなかなかいない。",
      "english": "It's hard to find a person truly worthy of respect.",
      "notes": null,
      "has_audio": false,
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{足|た}る is a classical/literary form meaning 'to be sufficient' or 'to be worthy of.' In modern Japanese, the ichidan verb {足|た}りる is more commonly used for the meaning 'to be enough.'\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: Intransitive ({自動詞|じどうし})\n- Pattern: Xに{足|た}る (worthy of X)\n\nMODERN USAGE:\n{足|た}る is mainly used in formal/literary expressions, especially in the pattern 「～に{足|た}る」(worthy of ~).\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- ～に{足|た}る (worthy of ~, deserving of ~)\n- {信頼|しんらい}に{足|た}る (worthy of trust)\n- {注目|ちゅうもく}に{足|た}る (worthy of attention)\n- {言及|げんきゅう}に{足|た}る (worth mentioning)\n\nCOMPARISON:\n- {足|た}る: Classical/literary, used in 「～に{足|た}る」\n- {足|た}りる: Modern, used for 'to be enough'",
